    "Pinned original Video calls queue helpers out of line, while queue set_limit/append/allocate inline clear/discard free paths. Queue constructor/six implementation methods lie at63E520..63E85B while its destructor6381E0 is emitted beside Video. AlphaMovie similarly calls ordinary MCI methods at5FFD80..600326 while the MCI destructor4042C0 belongs to its application cleanup group. Address adjacency alone establishes neither filenames nor Jackal ownership.",
    "Fresh private source/header overlay controls preserve all current33Video+30Alpha legacy verdicts and independent reviewers confirm all ten Video helper edges, original Video destructor118-byte opcode sequence/five targets/state3,2,1,0,-1, both four-state EH tables and queue-destructor cleanup targets. MCI split restores AlphaMovie destructor close/base-close/close/palette/base-dtor order and retained cold MCI destructor copies. Unchanged-replica full-function controls and damaged-constructor controls pass; these private observations are not production or full-span acceptance.",
    "Transfer seven unchanged VideoFrameQueue constructor/method definitions and complete mappings/claims/lessons into src/video_queue.cpp. Put the unchanged queue destructor body inline in video.h and retain its canonical mapping in video.cpp with native body fact. Transfer ten unchanged MCIVideo ordinary/callback/helper definitions and the ActiveVideoPlayer/MciVideoCallbackWindow definitions plus intact original object bindings into src/mci_video.cpp. Put unchanged MCI destructor body inline in alphamovie.h, canonical mapping remains alphamovie.cpp with native body fact. Keep existing AlphaMovie::close non-inline and emitted; do not add exports, forced references, noinline attributes, copied code or explicit extra member destruction. Existing blit_frame source remains general.cpp, in review scope but not edited.",
    "Restore default application Ob2 for video.cpp and alphamovie.cpp by removing only their source-local Ob1 CMake options. New units use that same unchanged global policy. Explicit diagnostic Ob2 contexts for these four units must reflect the actual build, not pick permissive alternatives. Preserve PullDown/DipEdit Ob1 and DipEdit Oy-, all global/compiler/linker/runtime policy, source order outside the two adjacent additions, class storage/layout, function bodies, original unsafe/error behavior, annotations, claims and unresolved findings. No real historical TU name or Jackal attribution is inferred.",
    "Authorized test changes only follow source/body homes and replace obsolete whole-project source/profile snapshots with durable live owner/global-policy controls. Preserve original body/annotation inverses and damage assertions for each test own owner; unrelated future TUs must not freeze recovery again. Adapt VideoSound inverse to only its actual owner, not an entire live Video source snapshot. Extend actual-source queue destructor behavior/damage control, keep MCI word-width/message/owner behavior controls. No blanket xfail, relaxed function coverage or unrelated test deletion.",
    "Only coordinator performs native compiler leases/Git/integration; disjoint source/test delegates freeze before measurements. Require fresh172-TU build/link, all64 subjects and original exact controls, moved symbol/reference/lifetime/data/unwind accounting, native complete object residuals/transport and source-history continuity, independent review and fresh destination verification. Any outside-scope discovery requests expansion before editing. No demotion, baseline reset, copied-body waiver, automatic acceptance or game/runtime claim. Native full-span constructor/destructor limitations remain unknown even when independent bounded primary-code evidence passes."
